ons, digital engagement centers, marketing campaigns, and user authentication and identity solutions. It also offers software products to build direct and personalized relationships with their end users, such as Segment, a platform that provides tools to harness the power of contextual data by unifying real-time information collected throughout each customer's journey into a unique profile. Twilio Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Khozema Zoher Shipchandler | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $901K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 38%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $177K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $107K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Twilio Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $32.7B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -12% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 52% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $997M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 29.65\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 234% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.34074995484707},{"text":"Goodwill represents 54% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $145.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Twilio Inc. $TWLO Shares Sold by Kestra Advisory Services LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/twilio-inc-twlo-shares-sold-by-kestra-advisory-services-llc.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566726.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Accelerated Revenue Growth Lifted Twilio (TWLO) in Q3","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/accelerated-revenue-growth-lifted-twilio-143734315.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794407854.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Twilio (NYSE:TWLO) Cooling From Highs?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technical-analysis/is-twilio-nysetwlo-cooling-from-highs","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3,164 Twilio Inc. $TWLO Shares Acquired by Illinois Municipal Retirement Fund","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/3164-twilio-inc-twlo-shares-acquired-by-illinois-municipal-retirement-fund.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794398109.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Should Earnings Beat Require Action From Twilio (TWLO) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nyse-twlo/twilio/news/should-earnings-beat-require-action-from-twilio-twlo-investo","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794372509.499,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company",